sequenceDiagram
    participant vLLM as vLLM / Bench
    participant LMC_I as LMCache<br/>(Initiator)
    participant LMC_T as LMCache<br/>(KV Cache Node)
    participant SSD as NVMe (L2)

    Note over vLLM,SSD: High-level target flow. See lmcache-ipu-pull-model-flow.mmd for wire-level detail<br/>(control frames, MR lifetime, two-phase eviction, lease and cancel semantics).

    Note over vLLM,SSD: === RETRIEVE ===

    vLLM->>LMC_I: retrieve(tokens)
    LMC_I->>LMC_T: request (keys + dst descriptor)
    alt HIT (L1 or L2)
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: RDMA Write into dst buffer
        LMC_I-->>vLLM: KV ready
    else MISS
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: miss
        LMC_I-->>vLLM: recompute KV
    end

    Note over vLLM,SSD: === STORE (Pull Model) ===

    vLLM->>LMC_I: store(tokens, kv)
    LMC_I->>LMC_I: prepare source buffer + BLAKE3 digest D
    LMC_I->>LMC_T: write intent (key, digest D)

    Note over LMC_T: Admission decision

    alt ALREADY_PRESENT (dedup)
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: ACK — idempotent success
    else REJECT (over-quota or fenced)
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: NACK
    else QUEUE (no capacity)
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: QUEUED — MR stays pinned
        alt capacity becomes available
            LMC_T-->>LMC_I: ACCEPT — continue to pull path
        else lease expires
            LMC_T-->>LMC_I: EXPIRE
            LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source buffer
        else initiator cancels
            LMC_I->>LMC_T: CANCEL
            LMC_T-->>LMC_I: CANCEL ACK
            LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source buffer
        end
    else ACCEPT (capacity available)
        Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Continue to pull path below
    end

    Note over LMC_T,SSD: For an ACCEPT (immediate or post-queue), target owns the pull

    LMC_T->>LMC_T: allocate L1 slot (evict LRU to L2 if L1 full)
    LMC_T-->>LMC_I: RDMA Read from initiator's source buffer
    LMC_T->>LMC_T: recompute BLAKE3 → validate against D

    alt VALIDATE OK
        LMC_T->>LMC_T: commit — publish (key → page)
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: store ACK (terminal)
        LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source buffer
    else VALIDATE FAIL
        LMC_T->>LMC_T: discard page (not published)
        LMC_T-->>LMC_I: NACK (integrity)
        LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source buffer
    end
